{
  "description": "Speaker-background layer wire contract, Qendresa item 18 extension (`focus` on the fill and on each window, capability `backgroundFocus`, protocol 42). A focus `{x, y, zoom}` places a photo/video background like VisualMediaPlacement: base scale = cover, drawn scale = max(cover * zoom, contain), `x`/`y` align the drawn picture (0 = left/top edge, 0.5 = centre, 1 = right/bottom edge). `x`,`y` in 0...1, `zoom` in 0.2...4.0, no other keys. A colour fill carries no focus (its windows may). `focus: null` is read as absent on both sides and never written. Every `valid` layer must decode (Python SpeakerBackgroundLayer, Swift SpeakerBackgroundLayer), equal its `normalized` form and re-encode to it; every `invalid` entry must be rejected by both. v1.json to v4.json still apply unchanged: a layer without the key serialises exactly as there.",
